issue.description:
Found while fixing the Ctrl+Shift+B cursor/viewport jump (bob-navigation-hotkeys 2.45.2). Repo: bob-plugins (linked); pre-existing, not caused by that change.

`planCountedLocalTaskDependency` (`plugins/bob-navigation-hotkeys/src/270-counted-batches.js`) processes the counted sources bottom-to-top and assumes "edits only shift lines below the current parent, so every still-pending source retains its snapshot index". That stopped being true once Depends-On writes mirror a generated `🧱 BLOCKS:` line under a same-note prerequisite: when the prerequisite is *above* the sources, planning the lowest source inserts a BLOCKS line above the remaining sources and shifts them down, so their snapshot `target.line` now points at the wrong line.

Reproduction (Node, `scripts/navigation-dependencies-stage-harness.cjs` helpers):

```js
const content = ["- [ ] #task Target ^target", "- [ ] #task First ^first", "- [ ] #task Second ^second"].join("\n");
const session = { explicit: true, targets: [
  { line: 1, rawLine: "- [ ] #task First ^first" },
  { line: 2, rawLine: "- [ ] #task Second ^second" } ] };
helpers.planCountedLocalTaskDependency(content, session,
  { line: 0, rawLine: "- [ ] #task Target ^target", existingIdField: null, existingBlockId: "target" },
  "Tasks.md", { blocksLinesEnabled: true, vaultFiles: ["Tasks.md"], resolveLinkpath: () => "Tasks.md" });
// -> { valid: false, error: "Could not plan dependency navigation for every source task" }
// with blocksLinesEnabled: false the same call succeeds and links both sources.
```

In the real gesture (`N<Ctrl+Shift+B>` on two sources below one same-note prerequisite, `dependencies.blocks_lines` on, the default) the user sees "Could not plan dependency navigation for every source task" and nothing is written.

The vault/cross-note counted writers in `src/420-picker-counted-dependency.js` (~l.333 and ~l.603) have the same class of problem for the freshness stamp: they call `stampDependencyParentLine(nextWorking, target.line)` at the pre-write line even though the plan may have shifted the dependent (`plan.parentLineNext` is the post-plan line; `applyDependencyEdit` in `580-plugin-properties-and-dependency-edit.js` already uses it).

Fix direction: thread each pending source's line through the accumulated line edits (`mapLineThroughLineEdits` / `plan.parentLineNext`) instead of reusing snapshot indexes, stamp at `plan.parentLineNext`, and add counted tests with the prerequisite above the sources.
